{{!-- ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
     members/app-link.hbs — the way through to app.namastesalesforce.com
     ------------------------------------------------------------------------
     The site and the app are two products sharing one design system: this Ghost
     theme is the public surface (courses, docs, training, the blog) and the
     Next.js LMS at app.namastesalesforce.com is where a signed-in member
     actually works through a lesson. This partial is the seam, and it exists
     once so that seam is consistent — a hand-written <a> to the app in nine
     templates is nine places to forget the target, the label, or the setting
     that turns it off.

     Params
       style   "btn" (default) · "outline" · "quiet" · "menu" — how it renders.
       block   truthy for a full-width button.
       label   override the label. Defaults to @custom.app_label.

     The URL is @custom.app_url (Ghost Admin → Design), so a fork of this theme
     points at its own app — or at nothing, in which case this renders nothing
     rather than a dead link to somebody else's product.

     Not target="_blank": the app is the same product, not an outbound link,
     and a new tab per lesson is how a learner ends up with fourteen of them. --}}

{{#if @custom.app_url}}
  {{#match style "menu"}}
    <a href="{{@custom.app_url}}" role="menuitem" class="ns-menu__item ns-menu__item--brand">
      {{> icons name="rocket" class="h-4 w-4"}}{{#if label}}{{label}}{{else}}{{@custom.app_label}}{{/if}}
    </a>
  {{else}}
    <a href="{{@custom.app_url}}"
       class="ns-btn {{#match style "outline"}}ns-btn--outline{{else}}{{#match style "quiet"}}ns-btn--ghost{{else}}ns-btn--primary{{/match}}{{/match}}{{#if block}} ns-btn--block{{/if}}">
      {{> icons name="rocket"}}{{#if label}}{{label}}{{else}}{{@custom.app_label}}{{/if}}
    </a>
  {{/match}}
{{/if}}
